<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-stringo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, strictum, 3,
				v. a. (post-class.). * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To bind about</i>, <i>to put on</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid alicui rei: habitus cervicibus
					circumstrictus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To tie around</i>, <i>to
			surround</i>, <i>clothe with</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid aliquā re: pallium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Cor. Mil. 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>